Library\"},{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/\",\"title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is\"},{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/\",\"title\":\"Chapter Ten: The Opulence of the Absolute\"}],\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/8/\",\"bb\":2548,\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"pager\":{\"previous\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/7/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 7\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]},\"next\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/9/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 9\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":2878,\"bb\":568248,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/8/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"अहं सर्वस्य प्रभवो मत्त: सर्वं प्रवर्तते ।
इति मत्वा भजन्ते मां बुधा भावसमन्विता: ॥ ८ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2879,\"bb\":2549,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/8/b2549/\",\"body_value\":\"ahaṁ sarvasya prabhavo
mattaḥ sarvaṁ pravartate
iti matvā bhajante māṁ
budhā bhāva-samanvitāḥ\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2880,\"bb\":2550,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/8/b2550/\",\"shadow_value\":\"aham – I; sarvasya – of all; prabhavaḥ – the source of generation; mattaḥ – from Me; sarvam – everything; pravartate – emanates; iti – thus; matvā – knowing; bhajante – become devoted; mām – unto Me; budhāḥ – the learned; bhāva-samanvitāḥ – with great attention.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"aham\",\"translation\":\"I\"},{\"word\":\"sarvasya\",\"translation\":\"of all\"},{\"word\":\"prabhavaḥ\",\"translation\":\"the source of generation\"},{\"word\":\"mattaḥ\",\"translation\":\"from Me\"},{\"word\":\"sarvam\",\"translation\":\"everything\"},{\"word\":\"pravartate\",\"translation\":\"emanates\"},{\"word\":\"iti\",\"translation\":\"thus\"},{\"word\":\"matvā\",\"translation\":\"knowing\"},{\"word\":\"bhajante\",\"translation\":\"become devoted\"},{\"word\":\"mām\",\"translation\":\"unto Me\"},{\"word\":\"budhāḥ\",\"translation\":\"the learned\"},{\"word\":\"bhāva-samanvitāḥ\",\"translation\":\"with great attention\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2881,\"bb\":2551,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/8/b2551/\",\"body_value\":\"I am the source of all spiritual and material worlds. Everything emanates from Me. The wise who perfectly know this engage in My devotional service and worship Me with all their hearts.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2882,\"bb\":2552,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/8/b2552/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2883,\"bb\":2553,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/8/b2553/\",\"body_value\":\"It is said in the same Vedas, brahmaṇyo devakī-putraḥ: “The son of Devakī, Kṛṣṇa, is the Supreme Personality.” (Nārāyaṇa Upaniṣad 4) Then it is said, eko vai nārāyaṇa āsīn na brahmā neśāno nāpo nāgni-somau neme dyāv-āpṛthivī na nakṣatrāṇi na sūryaḥ: “In the beginning of the creation there was only the Supreme Personality Nārāyaṇa. There was no Brahmā, no Śiva, no water, no fire, no moon, no heaven and earth, no stars in the sky, no sun.” (Mahā Upaniṣad 1.2) In the Mahā Upaniṣad it is also said that Lord Śiva was born from the forehead of the Supreme Lord. Thus the Vedas say that it is the Supreme Lord, the creator of Brahmā and Śiva, who is to be worshiped.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2884,\"bb\":2554,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/8/b2554/\",\"body_value\":\"In the Mokṣa-dharma section of the Mahābhārata, Kṛṣṇa also says,\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2885,\"bb\":2555,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/8/b2555/\",\"body_value\":\"prajāpatiṁ ca rudraṁ cāpy
aham eva sṛjāmi vai
tau hi māṁ na vijānīto
mama māyā-vimohitau\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2886,\"bb\":2556,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/8/b2556/\",\"body_value\":\"“The patriarchs, Śiva and others are created by Me, though they do not know that they are created by Me because they are deluded by My illusory energy.” In the Varāha Purāṇa it is also said,\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2887,\"bb\":2557,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/8/b2557/\",\"body_value\":\"nārāyaṇaḥ paro devas
tasmāj jātaś caturmukhaḥ
tasmād rudro ’bhavad devaḥ
sa ca sarva-jñatāṁ gataḥ\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2888,\"bb\":2558,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/8/b2558/\",\"body_value\":\"“Nārāyaṇa is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and from Him Brahmā was born, from whom Śiva was born.”\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2889,\"bb\":2559,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/8/b2559/\",\"body_value\":\"Lord Kṛṣṇa is the source of all generations, and He is called the most efficient cause of everything. He says, “Because everything is born of Me, I am the original source of all. Everything is under Me; no one is above Me.” There is no supreme controller other than Kṛṣṇa. One who understands Kṛṣṇa in such a way from a bona fide spiritual master, with references from Vedic literature, engages all his energy in Kṛṣṇa consciousness and becomes a truly learned man. In comparison to him, all others, who do not know Kṛṣṇa properly, are but fools. Only a fool would consider Kṛṣṇa to be an ordinary man. A Kṛṣṇa conscious person should not be bewildered by fools; he should avoid all unauthorized commentaries and interpretations on Bhagavad-gītā and proceed in Kṛṣṇa consciousness with determination and firmness.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 10.8\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 10.8\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.